Date: Tue, 13 Oct 2026 15:03:00 +0330
Subject: [PATCH 078/230] Stop reading a literal `+` in Telegram initData as a
 space
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

URLSearchParams applies form-encoding rules, so the `+` Telegram puts in a
signed field (base64 signature, start_param, a name) came back as a space.
That changes the bytes the server HMACs, so a genuine login was rejected and
the user silently landed on a guest account. Extract the launch params with a
manual `&`/`=` split + decodeURIComponent instead, and let the verifier read a
payload containing `+` under both readings (literal plus first, legacy
form-encoded second) so nothing that verified before stops verifying.

